"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"The Art of Tattooing\",\n      \"type\": \"Cultural Practice\",\n      \"description\": \"Tattooing is a form of art that has been practiced for centuries in various cultures around the world, evolving in meaning and acceptance over time.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Duration\": \"Centuries\",\n        \"Global Presence\": \"Practiced in various cultures around the world\",\n        \"Evolution\": \"Changing attitudes and meanings over time\",\n        \"Artistic Recognition\": \"Recognized as a form of art with evolving attitudes towards its display and acceptance\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Tattooing\",\n      \"type\": \"Cultural Practice\",\n      \"description\": \"Tattooing is a form of art and cultural practice that involves the insertion of ink into the skin to create permanent designs or images. It has a rich history dating back thousands of years and is practiced in various cultures around the world, often holding deep personal, social, and cultural meanings.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Historical Significance\": \"Dates back thousands of years, with evidence of tattooed mummies found in ancient Egypt, Asia, and Europe.\",\n        \"Cultural Role\": \"Played a significant role in cultures around the world, from ancient rituals to modern-day self-expression.\",\n        \"Artistic Nature\": \"Combines technical skill, creativity, and personal expression, making it a unique form of art.\",\n        \"Process\": \"Involves the insertion of ink into the skin to create permanent designs or images.\",\n        \"Social Perception\": \"Has seen a growing acceptance in mainstream society, helping to destigmatize tattoos and highlight their artistic and cultural significance.\",\n        \"Personal Significance\": \"Can hold deep personal meanings, such as commemorating a significant event or person, symbolizing resilience and strength, or serving as a form of self-empowerment and self-expression.\",\n        \"Professionalism\": \"Tattoo artists are skilled professionals who use a combination of technical expertise and creative vision to bring their clients\\\" ideas to life.\",\n        \"Communication Importance\": \"Communication is key in the tattooing process to ensure that both the artist and the client are on the same page regarding the design, placement, and overall outcome.\",\n        \"Styles and Techniques\": \"There is a wide range of styles and techniques, from traditional tribal designs to hyper-realistic portraits, allowing for unique and personalized tattoos.\",\n        \"Commitment Level\": \"Requires a certain level of commitment and trust, as the tattoo will be a permanent part of the individual\\\"s body.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"body decorations\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Body decorations refer to any form of adornment or modification applied to the human body, often for aesthetic, cultural, or personal reasons. Tattoos, a significant form of body decoration, are permanent designs that can hold deep personal and cultural meanings.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Purpose\": \"Aesthetic, Cultural, Personal\",\n        \"Form\": \"Permanent designs, Temporary modifications\",\n        \"Cultural Significance\": \"Symbols of status, spirituality, or protection in indigenous cultures; associated with the criminal underworld in Japan but later evolved into intricate designs symbolizing strength, courage, and tradition\",\n        \"Historical Context\": \"Dates back thousands of years, with evidence of tattooed mummies found in ancient Egypt, Asia, and Europe\",\n        \"Social Perception\": \"Evolution from stigma to growing acceptance in mainstream society\",\n        \"Styles and Techniques\": \"Wide range including traditional tribal designs, hyper-realistic portraits\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"hyper-realistic portraits\",\n      \"type\": \"Tattoo Style\",\n      \"description\": \"Hyper-realistic portraits are a style of tattoo that aims to replicate the detailed and lifelike appearance of a photograph or realistic image on the skin.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Style\": \"Hyper-realistic\",\n        \"Technique\": \"Detailed and lifelike replication of images\",\n        \"Subject\": \"Portraits\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Tattoos\",\n      \"type\": \"Body Art\",\n      \"description\": \"Tattoos are permanent designs or marks made on the skin by injecting ink, pigments, or dyes through the epidermis into the dermis layer of the skin.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Strength\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Strength refers to the quality or state of being physically or mentally strong.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Courage\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Courage is the ability to do something that frightens one.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Tradition\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Tradition refers to a custom or belief that is passed down through generations within a group or society.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Status Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Indicator\",\n      \"description\": \"A status symbol is an object or quality that is intended to show a person\\\"s social or economic status.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Spiritual Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"Religious Indicator\",\n      \"description\": \"A spiritual symbol is a visual representation of a spiritual concept or belief.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Protection Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"Cultural Indicator\",\n      \"description\": \"A protection symbol is a visual representation intended to provide protection or ward off harm.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Workplace Policies\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Norm\",\n      \"description\": \"Workplace policies are rules and guidelines established by employers to govern the behavior of employees.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Social Media Trends\",\n      \"type\": \"Cultural Phenomenon\",\n      \"description\": \"Social media trends are popular topics or behaviors that spread rapidly through social media platforms.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Japanese Tattooing\",\n      \"type\": \"Cultural Practice\",\n      \"description\": \"Japanese tattooing, or irezumi, is a traditional form of tattooing that has a rich history and cultural significance in Japan.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Tattoo Artists\",\n      \"type\": \"Profession\",\n      \"description\": \"Tattoo artists are skilled professionals who use a combination of technical expertise and creative vision to create tattoos.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Personal Expression\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Personal expression refers to the act of conveying one\\\"s thoughts, feelings, and identity through various means.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Cultural Identity\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Cultural identity is the sense of belonging to a particular culture or group, often expressed through shared values, traditions, and symbols.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Rite of Passage\",\n      \"type\": \"Cultural Practice\",\n      \"description\": \"A rite of passage is a ceremony or event marking a significant transition in a person\\\"s life, such as coming of age or marriage.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Status\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Concept\",\n      \"descr