manently adorn their bodies with meaningful designs.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Influences\",\n      \"Cultural Identity\",\n      \"Tattooing influences cultural identity, particularly in cultures where tattoos have traditional or symbolic meanings.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Symbolizes\",\n      \"Rite of Passage\",\n      \"In Polynesian cultures, tattooing symbolizes a rite of passage and a way to connect with one\\\"s ancestors.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Symbolizes\",\n      \"Status\",\n      \"In many indigenous cultures, tattooing symbolizes status, often indicating social standing or achievements.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Symbolizes\",\n      \"Spirituality\",\n      \"In many indigenous cultures, tattooing symbolizes spirituality, often used as a means to connect with the divine or spiritual realm.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Symbolizes\",\n      \"Protection\",\n      \"In many indigenous cultures, tattooing symbolizes protection, often believed to ward off evil or bring good fortune.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Associated With\",\n      \"Criminal Underworld\",\n      \"In Japan, tattooing was historically associated with the criminal underworld, though this perception has evolved over time.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Associated With\",\n      \"Mainstream Society\",\n      \"Tattooing has become increasingly associated with mainstream society, reflecting a shift in social attitudes and acceptance.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Influences\",\n      \"Workplace Policies\",\n      \"Tattooing influences workplace policies, with many workplaces now allowing visible tattoos, reflecting a broader acceptance of tattoos in professional settings.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Tattooing\",\n      \"Influences\",\n      \"Social Media\",\n      \"Tattooing influences social media, where celebrities and influencers proudly display their tattoos, contributing to the normalization and appreciation of tattoos.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"body decorations\",\n      \"Includes\",\n      \"tattoos\",\n      \"Tattoos are a form of body decoration that can be both aesthetic and deeply meaningful.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"body decorations\",\n      \"Associated With\",\n      \"artistry\",\n      \"Tattoos are recognized for the artistry involved in their creation, reflecting the skill of the tattoo artist.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"body decorations\",\n      \"Recognized In\",\n      \"mainstream society\",\n      \"The perception of tattoos as body decorations has evolved, leading to growing acceptance in mainstream society.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"body decorations\",\n      \"Displayed By\",\n      \"celebrities and influencers\",\n      \"Celebrities and influencers often display their tattoos on social media, contributing to the normalization and appreciation of body decorations.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"body decorations\",\n      \"Allowed In\",\n      \"workplaces\",\n      \"Many workplaces now allow visible tattoos, reflecting a shift in attitudes towards body decorations.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"body decorations\",\n      \"Created By\",\n      \"tattoo artists\",\n      \"Tattoos, as a form of body decoration, are created by tattoo artists who collaborate with their clients to ensure the design is both aesthetically pleasing and meaningful.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"hyper-realistic portraits\",\n      \"Is a Type of\",\n      \"tattoo\",\n      \"Hyper-realistic portraits are a specific type of tattoo that focuses on creating highly detailed and lifelike images.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"hyper-realistic portraits\",\n      \"Created By\",\n      \"tattoo artists\",\n      \"Hyper-realistic portraits are created by tattoo artists who have the necessary skills and expertise to produce such detailed and lifelike designs.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"hyper-realistic 